 response←request RedirectToDocs path
⍝ Answers a request for a page of the documentation Tatin used to serve itself with a
⍝ permanent redirect to wherever that page lives now; see `GetDocsUrl`.
⍝ Those pages were served from a "docs/" folder in the root of the server until the
⍝ documentation moved to aplteam.github.io. The folder went, the links to it did not, and
⍝ they have been answered with a 404 ever since.
⍝ 301 rather than 302 on purpose: the move is permanent, so a search engine should pass
⍝ whatever standing the old URL had on to the new one instead of keeping both.
 response←request Respond 301
 response.Headers,←⊂'Location'(GetDocsUrl path)
⍝Done
